==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|sylky}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|silk|y}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɪlki/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪlki}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# Similar in [[appearance]] or [[texture]] (especially in [[softness]] and [[smoothness]]) to [[silk]].
#: ''cloth with a '''silky''' lustre''
#: '''''silky''' hair''
# [[smooth|Smooth]] and [[pleasant]]; [[seductive]].
#: ''a '''silky''' wine''
#: ''a '''silky''' voice''
#: '''''silky''' skills''
# {{lb|en|botany}} Covered in long, slender, glistening hairs pressed close to the surface; [[sericeous]].

